       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2550 mg three times daily, which is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Why it's a problem:** The maximum labeled metformin dose is 2,550 mg/day for adults. This order is 3 times that, and it risks severe lactic acidosis. A single 2,550 mg dose also exceeds the usual per-dose maximum of about 1,000 mg.\n\nYou may have meant 2,550 mg total per day, which is **850 mg three times daily with meals**. Or you may have intended a different dose.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. For example, I can enter metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals. If you really intend the original dose, tell me and I'll enter it as written."
